---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The Unhurried Traveler"
  description="Who writes this, why the journeys are solo, and why the best travel of a lifetime can start after sixty."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-36">
    <SectionHeading eyebrow="About" title="Alone by choice, unhurried by conviction" />

    <div class="prose-journal mt-10">
      <p>
        I took my first solo trip at an age when most travel writing assumes you've hung up your boots.
        My wife of many years had gone; the children were grown and scattered; and the choice, it turned out,
        was between a smaller life and a larger one. I bought a one-way ticket to Lisbon, packed one bag,
        and discovered something nobody had told me: <strong>Europe is the easiest place in the world to be
        alone, and being alone is the most underrated way to see it.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is the notebook from everything since — the cliff villages of the Dordogne, the little red
        trains of the Alps, milk-bar lunches in Kraków, October swims below the Cinque Terre. I travel slowly,
        stay in one place at a time, ride trains where I can, and film what I see with a pocket camera and a
        drone that weighs less than a paperback.
      </p>
      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Journal</strong> — long-form field notes: routes, architecture, history, and the practical craft of solo travel at a certain age.</li>
        <li><strong>The Chart</strong> — an interactive map of every journey, with honest notes on season and walking pace.</li>
        <li><strong>The Kit</strong> — the one-bag setup, from trekking poles to the flying camera.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The honesty clause</h2>
      <p>
        A few entries mention partners who help keep the site running; they're always labelled, they never
        see an entry before publication, and nothing appears here that I don't carry, use, or stand behind.
        If a famous village is overrated, I'll say so — and tell you what time of year makes it worth it anyway.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        Alone never meant lonely. It means every cathedral gets the time it deserves, every wrong turn is
        allowed, and lunch lasts exactly as long as it wants to.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        If you're standing where I stood — retired, on your own, wondering whether the big trip is still
        possible — consider this site one long letter saying: <em>yes, and go in the shoulder season.</em>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a
        href={withBase('/blog/')}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-accent-600 px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-accent-600/25 transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-accent-500"
      >
        Start with the journal
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
      </a>
      <a
        href="mailto:wefeltlikeit@gmail.com"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-brand-800/20 px-6 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-800 transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-accent-500 hover:text-accent-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-paper/85 dark:hover:text-accent-400"
      >
        Write to me
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
